WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.386
Two hundred and twenty-nine million dollars.

00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:06.238
That is the documented value of the Canadian arms pipeline to Israel.

00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:09.534
Eighteen point nine million exported in 2024.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:13.829
Thirty-seven point two million in new permits issued in 2025.

00:00:13.829 --> 00:00:20.886
Seventy-eight point eight million in a single General Dynamics artillery contract signed September 26th, 2024.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:24.159
Ninety-four point five million in remaining active permits.

00:00:24.159 --> 00:00:26.011
The government announced a pause.

00:00:26.011 --> 00:00:27.636
The pipeline never stopped.

00:00:27.636 --> 00:00:33.897
Two thousand one hundred and fifty-six lobbying communications from CIJA — the Centre for Israel and Jewish Affairs.

00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:41.761
One thousand and seventy-nine from David Pratt alone — four hundred and eight to the Department of National Defence, one hundred and thirty-nine to the PMO.

00:00:41.761 --> 00:00:48.420
Post-October 7th, lobbying surged two hundred and thirty-nine percent to three hundred and ninety communications.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:54.465
Seventy-three Members of Parliament accepted paid trips to Israel costing eight hundred and ninety-four thousand dollars.

00:00:54.465 --> 00:01:00.784
Bill C-233 — the arms embargo bill — was defeated twenty-two to two hundred and ninety-five.

00:01:00.784 --> 00:01:02.738
The pipeline is not a secret.

00:01:02.738 --> 00:01:03.954
It is a policy.
